    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 219,
        "text": "Okay, everyone, thanks for coming. Let's start with the community center project. The brief says the new reading room must be open to all ages and abilities. So, inclusion is not an extra; it's the starting point.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "6fb96e3d7012bd26087c7c7c0164a042162fb96f4b0b70b075eff868820569f7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 226,
        "sourceEnd": 486,
        "text": "Right. I looked at the entrance. The current door is 900 millimeters wide. That's too narrow for many wheelchairs. We need at least 1,000 millimeters. And the ramp—the slope is 1 in 8. That's steeper than the standard 1 in 12. So we have two clear constraints.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "5e68b6c57ab72109bb9b23e32c93c8b54b2db1d5327fab231fd6f264409e6d74",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 494,
        "sourceEnd": 568,
        "text": "Good. So the door and the ramp are non-negotiable. What about the signage?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "d9b3cbbda59deeefc214ea815f52daceb8824cb528d0c4606a7ae2814743182c",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 575,
        "sourceEnd": 746,
        "text": "The signs are all text. For people with low vision, we need high contrast and maybe braille. But braille adds cost. I'm not saying we skip it—I'm saying we need to decide.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "c410477987124f59a33467f7453b333a5e2d06b09cc135c5b5761814cd4c83a3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 755,
        "sourceEnd": 963,
        "text": "Can I add something? The lighting matters as much as the signs. If the room is too bright, some people with autism find it uncomfortable. We could use dimmable lights. That's a small change with a big effect.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "d1b0b2486a5e9b123666945bffed8adec7c80c93de2e63fc916a0725afc8f846",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 971,
        "sourceEnd": 1214,
        "text": "I like that. So, to summarize: door width, ramp slope, signage, and lighting. Four design constraints. Now, the budget. We have 20,000 dollars for the whole room. The door and ramp will take about 12,000. That leaves 8,000 for everything else.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "139b42978ab7138a1ef2717dc3ad42167160a104f621e15166c34b8315e81e47",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1221,
        "sourceEnd": 1322,
        "text": "Wait—I said 12,000, but that was an old quote. The new quote is 13,500. Sorry. So we have 6,500 left.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "d24f3621340414b10d13f66cd8881e5d461f961d7612f15b76562e0073459c87",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1330,
        "sourceEnd": 1411,
        "text": "Thanks for the correction. That changes things. Priya, how much for the lighting?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "18914931d5d43ad278b89ad41a0a3678ae5f46c8089c7d641c2e387fca126f53",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 1420,
        "sourceEnd": 1526,
        "text": "Dimmable lights are about 2,000. Braille signs are 1,500. That's 3,500. We still have 3,000 for furniture.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "fa1c9092073693f67954e4f079ade285fc046bf504a6f26c54cfadfaa47568d7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1533,
        "sourceEnd": 1631,
        "text": "But we also need a hearing loop for the front desk. That's another 1,200. So furniture gets 1,800.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "4df36b853d339fd7394e47d19fb277afac70e0967a6978416cf834b3970110aa",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1639,
        "sourceEnd": 1855,
        "text": "Okay. So the final numbers: 13,500 for access, 2,000 for lighting, 1,500 for signs, 1,200 for the hearing loop, and 1,800 for furniture. That totals 20,000 exactly. Good. Now, who will check the measurements on site?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "7f403ba80376b9f2b82a2b54df2cd57a3dd6f0b8882ac517d3da8a24bbeb2108",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leo",
        "speaker": "Leo",
        "sourceStart": 1862,
        "sourceEnd": 1918,
        "text": "I can do that on Thursday. I'll bring the laser measure.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-ChristopherNeural",
        "textHash": "151b8cfc99a9eb9b6decc88a21430895546d602c39de6f2836a935b7f940505b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "priya",
        "speaker": "Priya",
        "sourceStart": 1927,
        "sourceEnd": 1988,
        "text": "And I'll contact the braille supplier. I'll ask for a sample.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
        "textHash": "8654bcc270679b48bd64d5c501badf1b2bfdfcbc6f68b14c2d7c1809e79b27c0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "maya",
        "speaker": "Maya",
        "sourceStart": 1996,
        "sourceEnd": 2147,
        "text": "Perfect. So next steps: Leo checks measurements, Priya gets a sample, and I'll update the budget sheet. Let's meet again next Monday. Thanks, everyone.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-MichelleNeural",
        "textHash": "45b125461819101833fd05fc352a3947cb15a876b0d833e8cf2aea9dcd52d592",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
